 "note": "For each example we read label_count (per-label votes, sum 100), the original gold old_label, and ChaosNLI's majority_label (a plurality / argmax). strict_majority = a label with strictly more than half (> 50) of the 100 votes; plurality = the unique argmax (a tie at the top -> none). n_old_differs_majority verifies ChaosNLI's documented old-vs-plurality disagreement (378 SNLI / 508 MNLI). n_no_strict_majority counts examples where even 100 fresh annotators reach no strict majority, yet the benchmark assigns one hard gold label; n_old_on_no_strict counts how many of those still carry an old gold. n_majority_eq_plurality checks that ChaosNLI's majority_label equals our recomputed argmax. P1 verifies the documented disagreement counts; P2 that every label_count sums to 100; P3 (direction only, exact count reported) that a nonzero number of examples lack a strict 100-vote majority. alphaNLI is reported (2-choice) but not bet on; headline predictions are on the two 3-way subsets."
}